WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.583 --> 00:00:01.626
(BIRDS CHIRPING)

00:00:01.710 --> 00:00:04.003
Hey y'all. We are back
and we are so excited

00:00:04.087 --> 00:00:07.340
to wine down and talk
about this wild episode,

00:00:07.424 --> 00:00:08.299
"High-Like."

00:00:08.675 --> 00:00:11.511
And our very own Yvonne Orji
is back with us this week

00:00:11.594 --> 00:00:13.596
-to get into it.
-Yeah!

00:00:16.683 --> 00:00:19.102
This weekend was supposed to be
about two things,

00:00:19.185 --> 00:00:20.979
female bonding and Beyoncé.

00:00:21.271 --> 00:00:23.857
This was meant to be like
a girls-fun episode.

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:25.650
It was our first time,
this season,

00:00:25.942 --> 00:00:28.570
that we really got to get
everybody together.

00:00:28.653 --> 00:00:30.780
Episode three was like a nice,
little cute, little dinner.

00:00:31.030 --> 00:00:33.783
But this was like,
the girls in their element.

00:00:33.867 --> 00:00:35.368
-PRENTICE PENNY: Totally.
-Beyoncé or bust.

00:00:35.452 --> 00:00:36.619
Beyoncé or bust!

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:38.997
If you're not
in your Beyoncé mode,

00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:40.165
you're just busting in life.

00:00:40.248 --> 00:00:41.499
You're bust-- You're losing.

00:00:41.583 --> 00:00:42.667
-Ooh!
-Like, why would you--

00:00:42.751 --> 00:00:44.294
-With the elongated "oohs?"
-ISSA RAE: Yeah.

00:00:44.377 --> 00:00:46.713
It's like what would Jesus do
on Beyoncé or bust? Kinda like--

00:00:46.796 --> 00:00:48.047
-Yeah, Beyoncé or bust.
-Copy.

00:00:48.256 --> 00:00:49.799
I think it's the first time
that we actually see the girls

00:00:49.883 --> 00:00:51.926
have a little bit of a hiccup
in their relationship.

00:00:52.010 --> 00:00:53.428
'Cause usually,
when the girls are together,

00:00:53.511 --> 00:00:56.139
either Issa or Molly is bringing
a problem to the group,

00:00:56.222 --> 00:00:58.391
and the group is sorta weighing
in on those discussions.

00:00:58.641 --> 00:01:00.226
What we always talked about,
is like, how do we see

00:01:00.310 --> 00:01:02.061
-new dynamics of friendships?
-Yeah.

00:01:02.145 --> 00:01:05.315
And it was nice to have that
Issa-Tiffany scene,

00:01:05.398 --> 00:01:07.776
where it was just them
in the parking lot of 7/11.

00:01:07.984 --> 00:01:10.236
We see Tiffany kinda be boujee
and throw a little shade.

00:01:10.487 --> 00:01:11.321
But it was really nice.

00:01:11.821 --> 00:01:13.114
I thought Amanda did such
an amazing job in that scene.

00:01:13.198 --> 00:01:14.491
-Yeah.
-And you guys both

00:01:14.824 --> 00:01:16.785
of being like,
"Aw, she's a real person.

00:01:16.868 --> 00:01:18.578
She's really having concerns
and doubts.

00:01:18.661 --> 00:01:21.039
And when she's not holding court
amongst all those things,

00:01:21.122 --> 00:01:23.041
this is how she really is
and really feels."

00:01:23.124 --> 00:01:24.250
And to me it made me understand,

00:01:24.334 --> 00:01:25.543
"Oh, that's why they're friends
with her."

00:01:25.627 --> 00:01:26.669
-Yeah.
-ISSA: And Tiffany,

00:01:27.003 --> 00:01:29.422
we get to see her in a rare,
vulnerable moment of just like,

00:01:29.506 --> 00:01:31.841
"Maybe I have to ask myself
if I'm okay with the fact that

00:01:31.925 --> 00:01:33.843
we might not be friends
further."

00:01:33.927 --> 00:01:35.595
-And to put that out there.
-Things will be different.

00:01:35.678 --> 00:01:37.847
Things will be different
and I have to be okay with that.

00:01:37.931 --> 00:01:39.641
And I think girls do that more
than guys,

00:01:39.724 --> 00:01:41.267
'cause you'll see a group
of dudes, you'll be like,

00:01:41.351 --> 00:01:42.435
"Why're you still friends
with him?" He be like,

00:01:42.852 --> 00:01:44.687
"Aw man, I've known him since
I was eight." Well, un-know him!

00:01:44.771 --> 00:01:46.940
-(LAUGHTER)
-Real talk, since you're a man,

00:01:47.023 --> 00:01:48.733
and a real man does wear
this scarf.

00:01:48.817 --> 00:01:51.486
I'm a man-- I'm a
bandana-wearing man. A real man.

00:01:51.820 --> 00:01:54.739
Why do guys not...
exchange friends

00:01:54.823 --> 00:01:56.866
when they make, like,
real-life decisions?

00:01:57.325 --> 00:01:58.952
'Cause I think dudes feel
very loyal

00:01:59.035 --> 00:02:02.497
to people who knew them
when they kinda had nothing.

00:02:02.914 --> 00:02:04.290
I think this is where
men and women are different,

00:02:04.374 --> 00:02:05.625
and I think that's what's
interesting about our show,

00:02:05.708 --> 00:02:08.628
is that, I think,
men can have friendships that,

00:02:08.878 --> 00:02:11.464
they'll say "that's my boy,"
but we don't really talk.

00:02:11.548 --> 00:02:13.842
Where if a girl would say,
like "that's my girl," we talk.

00:02:13.925 --> 00:02:16.177
And so I think the relationships
feels charged,

00:02:16.261 --> 00:02:18.388
and more interesting
and more dynamic,

00:02:18.638 --> 00:02:20.807
in a way that I think
men's friendships on--

00:02:20.890 --> 00:02:22.058
-And certainly onscreen.
-Yeah.

00:02:22.141 --> 00:02:23.768
Like even Lawrence,
like Lawrence in our show

00:02:23.852 --> 00:02:26.271
of being a guy who was like--
got cheated on,

00:02:26.354 --> 00:02:28.356
kinda became introverted
as opposed to,

00:02:28.439 --> 00:02:29.983
if it was a woman,
they would talk it out,

00:02:30.066 --> 00:02:31.317
-and sorta say why did he--
-Yeah.

00:02:31.693 --> 00:02:33.069
-Like even in the museum
last season.
-Well, he tried to talk it out.

00:02:33.152 --> 00:02:34.863
-He did! And his boys--
-He didn't have friends who're--

00:02:34.946 --> 00:02:37.824
Will Lawrence ever have, like,
friends that are better?

00:02:37.907 --> 00:02:40.535
Like, like is that something
we can help him with?

00:02:40.618 --> 00:02:41.828
I think he has-- Chad's a--

00:02:41.911 --> 00:02:43.496
-Chad is not a good friend!
-Chad's a loyal dude.

00:02:43.580 --> 00:02:45.957
BOTH: He's loyal but he's not
a good friend.

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:48.376
Like Chad and Lawrence.
Why are they friends?

00:02:48.459 --> 00:02:50.169
Ooh, speaking of Lawrence.

00:02:50.253 --> 00:02:53.339
-He's back this episode.
-He came back this episode.

00:02:53.423 --> 00:02:56.050
And it's gonna be
very interesting to see,

00:02:56.259 --> 00:02:57.844
you know, what that means
for Issa, you know.

00:02:58.094 --> 00:03:01.598
What was that moment like when
you saw Lawrence at the store?

00:03:01.681 --> 00:03:03.850
Oh! It was, um...
It was a little reunion.

00:03:03.933 --> 00:03:06.185
I got like butterflies
in my stomach of just like,

00:03:06.269 --> 00:03:09.480
"Aw, he's back," because
Jay hadn't been on set.

00:03:09.564 --> 00:03:10.356
Yeah.

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:11.858
Dun-duh-duh, surprise!
We got ya!

00:03:11.941 --> 00:03:13.985
(LAUGHTER)

00:03:14.068 --> 00:03:15.445
-Folks was trippin'!
-It was.

00:03:15.528 --> 00:03:17.280
But seeing Chad
made my stomach turn.

00:03:17.363 --> 00:03:19.449
'Cause I really-- I love Neil,
hate Chad.

00:03:19.616 --> 00:03:21.951
But it was just--
It felt like a reunion and...

00:03:22.035 --> 00:03:23.745
um, we're gonna see
next episode what that means.

00:03:23.828 --> 00:03:25.580
But that was one of the things
we talked about too in the room,

00:03:25.663 --> 00:03:27.290
was like, when do we
reintroduce Lawrence?

00:03:27.373 --> 00:03:29.876
And when do we bring him back?
And I think what's interesting,

00:03:30.293 --> 00:03:31.794
is, I think it was last season,

00:03:31.878 --> 00:03:34.088
where it was like,
as soon as you get a guy,

00:03:34.172 --> 00:03:35.924
bloop-bloop, here comes the exes
popping up.

00:03:36.007 --> 00:03:36.799
BOTH: Yes! Yes!

00:03:37.383 --> 00:03:39.385
And that's really what happens,
is like you're here with Nathan,

00:03:39.469 --> 00:03:40.470
and then, bloop-bloop,

00:03:40.553 --> 00:03:42.096
-here's Lawrence!
-Here comes Lawrence.

00:03:42.180 --> 00:03:44.057
So, thanks for wining down
with us this week,

00:03:44.140 --> 00:03:46.768
and thanks to the lovely,
as always, Yvonne Orji.

00:03:46.976 --> 00:03:48.144
-Oh, thank you. Hey, boo!
-ISSA: Yes!

00:03:48.353 --> 00:03:51.731
Cheers, cheers, cheers,
and we will see you next time.

00:03:52.190 --> 00:03:54.067
So, I have a question.
Is that a bandana? Are you--

00:03:54.150 --> 00:03:56.569
You know what? We don't need
to get into what this is.

00:03:56.653 --> 00:03:58.112
-It's just--
-Are you Bloods or Crips?

00:03:58.196 --> 00:03:59.405
You know what? I'm neutral.

00:03:59.489 --> 00:04:01.240
-(CHUCKLING) Is that what it is?
-I ride both sides.

00:04:01.324 --> 00:04:03.534
You know what? This is--
(MUTTERING)

00:04:03.618 --> 00:04:04.953
(CACKLING)

00:04:05.036 --> 00:04:06.829
-Prentice, come back!
-(PRENTICE SHOUTING)

